#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Harvest candidate commentary works for scripture passages.

The harvest itself consults a model, which is not reproducible. Exactly one
verb here does that; everything else is deterministic, and the nondeterminism
stays visible in the ledger, where the model identity and date are recorded
alongside what it said.

  plan     passages still needing harvest, as a worklist
  ask      the model, for one worklist, N times over  <- the only outward verb
  record   one run's results into the ledger, validated
  aliases  derive the tracked work-alias table from the ledger, validated
  promote  the ledger into the discovery index, confidence = appearances / runs

Until 2026-07-31 this tool called no model at all and the harvest was run by
hand outside it. That was not free: the identity and date `record` stamps were
whatever an operator typed, which is the failure this repository treats as
worst — a reference that resolves successfully and wrongly. `ask` closes that
gap by taking both from the answer itself, and the deterministic verbs stay
deterministic: `ask` writes nothing but a results file that `record` ingests.
"""
